      "page_idx": 9,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.57,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "A Tale of Three Intersecting Lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.088,
            0.74,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": "Does a triangle exist with sidelengths 4 cm, 5 cm and 8 cm?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.117,
            0.542,
            0.138
          ],
          "content": "This satisfies the triangle inequality:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.438,
            0.147,
            0.561,
            0.166
          ],
          "content": "8 < 4 + 5 = 9",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.181,
            0.649,
            0.204
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Why do we not need to check the other two sides?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.213,
            0.848,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": "This means that all the direct path lengths are less than the roundabout path lengths. Does this confirm the existence of a triangle?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.251,
            0.848,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": "If one of the direct path lengths had been longer, we could have concluded that a triangle would surely not exist. But in this case, we can only say that a triangle may or may not exist."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.306,
            0.849,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": "For the triangle to exist, the arcs that we construct to get the third without actually carrying out the construction?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.372,
            0.554,
            0.391
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Visualising the construction of circles"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.396,
            0.848,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": "Let us imagine that we start the construction by constructing the longest side as the base. Let AB be the base of length 8 cm. The next step is the construction of sufficiently long arcs corresponding to the other two lengths: 4 cm and 5 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.469,
            0.846,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": "Instead of just constructing the arcs, let us complete the full circles. Suppose, we construct a circle of radius 4 cm with A as the centre."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.512,
            0.747,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.773,
            0.846,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": "？ Now, suppose that a circle of radius 5 cm is constructed, centred at B. Can you draw a rough diagram of the resulting figure?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.823,
            0.848,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "Note that in the figure below, AX = 4 cm and AB = 8 cm. So, what is BX? Does this length help in visualising the resulting figure?"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
